<!--
  Firebase stub resources — see Sentry TUCOPWALLET-8 crash chain.

  The wallet's package.json pulls @react-native-firebase/app + analytics
  transitively via @segment/analytics-react-native-plugin-firebase, which
  brings the Android FirebaseInitProvider ContentProvider into the merged
  manifest. On app startup that provider tries to read `google_app_id`
  from res/values/; when it is missing FirebaseApp stays uninitialized,
  and any later native module (e.g. @react-native-firebase/dynamic-links
  onNewIntent, messaging listener, remote-config early access) that calls
  FirebaseApp.getInstance() throws
    IllegalStateException: Default FirebaseApp is not initialized in this process
  — a fatal native crash that surfaced as Sentry TUCOPWALLET-8 (19 users
  affected in the 1.118.10 rollout window, PENDING.md 2026-08-01 entry).

  Providing a syntactically valid but placeholder `google_app_id` here
  makes FirebaseInitProvider register a "default" FirebaseApp so
  getInstance() returns an app object instead of throwing. Any JS-side
  Firebase call that ends up hitting the network (dynamic links resolve,
  remote-config fetch, etc) will fail with a JS-catchable 401/403
  instead of a native uncaught IllegalStateException — the wallet's
  FirebaseDisabledError guards (src/firebase/dynamicLinks.ts) already
  handle those cases.

  This is the Option C hotfix from PENDING.md — cheapest fix that stops
  the crash bleed today. The strategic follow-up (Option A: wire real
  Firebase project, or Option B: remove @react-native-firebase modules
  outright since Firebase Dynamic Links is deprecated by Google in 2025)
  stays open and is tracked in the same PENDING entry. Do not treat this
  file as authorization to start using Firebase features from the app.

  The format of `google_app_id` is the standard Firebase mobile app id:
  `<project_number>:<platform_id>:<platform_short>:<app_hash>`. The
  values below are 0-filled placeholders; they satisfy the parser but
  do not point at any real Google project.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="google_app_id" translatable="false">1:000000000000:android:0000000000000000000000</string>
</resources>
